,"node_id":"IC_kwDOA0JFE86S9u2H","user":{"login":"richardfontana","id":1179636,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjExNzk2MzY=","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/1179636?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/richardfontana","html_url":"https://github.com/richardfontana","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/richardfontana/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/richardfontana/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/richardfontana/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/richardfontana/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/richardfontana/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/richardfontana/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/richardfontana/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/richardfontana/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/richardfontana/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2024-11-08T20:00:34Z","updated_at":"2024-11-08T20:06:34Z","body":"Note that the assertion here that \r\n\r\n> It is based on the Apache 2.0 license, with some exceptions. The exceptions specifically permit the re-packaging of the toolkit, and the distribution of such packages (e.g. as Fedora or Debian packages; see \"Toolkit Redistribution\" section of the exemption text). \r\n\r\nis possibly fundamentally incorrect and seems to be based in part on an interpretation of some unpublished communication with a representative of the licensor. See some discussion here:\r\nhttps://bugzilla.redhat.com/show_bug.cgi?id=2304835\r\n\r\nWhat does seem to be the case is that the JPL has adopted a general policy of using `Apache-2.0` for public source code releases, but the people at NAIF have evidently persuaded the powers that be there to grant them an exemption from the policy and thus avoid the impact of pro-open-source reform efforts within NASA. That's my take on it, anyway. \r\n\r\nThat's not to say that the NAIF-SPICE terms (whatever they actually are) aren't worthy of being represented with an SPDX identifier. ","author_association":"CONTRIBUTOR","pin":null,"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/spdx/license-list-XML/issues/comments/2465656199/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/spdx/license-list-XML/issues/comments/2656485713","html_url":"https://github.com/spdx/license-list-XML/issues/2612#issuecomment-2656485713","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/spdx/license-list-XML/issues/2612","id":2656485713,"node_id":"IC_kwDOA0JFE86eVsFR","user":{"login":"karsten-klein","id":20038021,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjIwMDM4MDIx","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/20038021?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/karsten-klein","html_url":"https://github.com/karsten-klein","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/karsten-klein/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/karsten-klein/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/karsten-klein/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/karsten-klein/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/karsten-klein/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/karsten-klein/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/karsten-klein/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/karsten-klein/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/karsten-klein/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2025-02-13T12:42:12Z","updated_at":"2025-02-13T12:42:12Z","body":"**Comment**\nWhat would we expect from a license scanner to detect here. A NAIF-SPICE marker? A \"license-policy\" marker?","author_ass